# golden-lifo

Does `tests/schedule_golden.rs` catch a schedule change? `run.sh` copies the tree at e9f73c3 (the 0.3.1
release) to a temp dir, runs the golden test, then gives `WakeOrdering::Lifo` the FIFO key in `order_key`
(`src/scope.rs` line 136) and runs it again.

    proofs/golden-lifo/run.sh

    == as released
    test result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; ...
    == with the change
    136c136
    <         WakeOrdering::Lifo => (0, 0, u64::MAX - e.runnable_seq),
    ---
    >         WakeOrdering::Lifo => (0, 0, e.runnable_seq),
    schedule changed; first differing line Some(753): now Some("poll 1 #0.0 y0"), recorded Some("poll 1 #11.0 y11")
    test result: FAILED. 0 passed; 1 failed; ...

`Some(753)` counts from 0, so the first differing line is line 754 of `tests/golden/schedule.txt`.
